# Phase 0 ingestion schedule (issue #68).
# Install with: crontab deploy/phase0-pipeline.cron
#
# TIMEZONE ASSUMPTION
# Every expression below is written in America/New_York and means nothing
# in any other zone: "every 30 minutes through 16:30" is a market-hours
# statement, not a wall-clock one. CRON_TZ is what makes that true, and it
# is honoured by Vixie cron and cronie only. On an implementation that
# ignores it -- busybox cron, some containers, macOS launchd wrappers --
# these lines silently run in host local time and the market window lands
# somewhere else. Verify before trusting the schedule:
#
#     grep CRON_TZ /var/log/syslog          # cron logged it, or it did not
#     date; TZ=America/New_York date        # host offset vs intended offset
#
# DST needs no handling here: America/New_York carries EST and EDT with it,
# so 09:30 stays 09:30 across both changeovers. A UTC schedule would drift
# by an hour twice a year, which is why one is not used.
CRON_TZ=America/New_York
SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# Replace these three for the deployment host.
PROJECT_DIR=/opt/ticker-narratives
PYTHON_BIN=/opt/ticker-narratives/.venv/bin/python
PHASE0_DATABASE_PATH=/var/lib/ticker-narratives/phase0.sqlite3

# OVERLAPPING INVOCATIONS
# A fetch can outlast its interval -- a slow provider, a retry budget, a
# large feed -- and cron starts the next copy regardless. Two live
# invocations then race for the same feeds and the same provider slots.
# `flock -n` refuses the second one immediately instead of queueing it
# behind a run that may itself be wedged; pipeline.py takes the same lock
# internally, so a manual or systemd invocation is covered too.
#
# EXIT CODES: 0 success (or skipped for overlap), 1 degraded, 2 failed.
# A degraded run persisted real evidence with some source incomplete, so
# alerting that treats every nonzero code as an outage will be noisy;
# alert on 2, and trend 1.

# Every 30 minutes from 09:00 through 16:30 ET on weekdays.
0,30 9-16 * * 1-5 cd $PROJECT_DIR && flock -n /var/lock/phase0-pipeline.lock $PYTHON_BIN pipeline.py >> /var/log/ticker-narratives-pipeline.log 2>&1

# Hourly outside the market-hour window: weekdays before 09:00 and after
# 16:30, plus every weekend hour.
0 0-8,17-23 * * 1-5 cd $PROJECT_DIR && flock -n /var/lock/phase0-pipeline.lock $PYTHON_BIN pipeline.py >> /var/log/ticker-narratives-pipeline.log 2>&1
0 * * * 0,6 cd $PROJECT_DIR && flock -n /var/lock/phase0-pipeline.lock $PYTHON_BIN pipeline.py >> /var/log/ticker-narratives-pipeline.log 2>&1
